From a69d0354a7a60519ce67a8a7188bd482480fa486 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 22:44:27 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] feat(vk_native): tell the person through
 sparky-stereo-problems when the window cannot be declared

When the runtime hands a stereo desktop compositor the two views side by side
and the declaration cannot be made (the desktop announces no stereo
declaration, an X11 window the runtime does not declare, a build without
wayland-scanner), the views are shown flat and the reason reached the log only.
With the option DXR_SPARKY_PROBLEMS (OFF by default, nothing changes for other
builds) the reason is kept as the person's problem through sparky-stereo-problems
and ended when the window is declared again or the display processor stops
asking. The engine's library is opened with dlopen at the first call, so the
runtime's linked libraries do not change; if it is absent the log says, as an
error, that the person could not be told. DXR_STEREO_DECLARE=0 is the person's
own choice and keeps no problem.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Origin: vendor, Sparky Stereo OS ORDER 58b
Forwarded: not-needed
Comment: The edition builds with DXR_SPARKY_PROBLEMS=ON: a window the runtime cannot declare is told to the person
 through sparky-stereo-problems (no silent fallback). The option is OFF by default and nothing changes for other builds.
Last-Update: 2026-11-09
